WEBVTT

1
00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:54.388
- Hey. Stuart.
- Bert.

2
00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.265
Got anything new?

3
00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.850
Funny every time.

4
00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:04.730
I think I'm ready to pull
the trigger on Batman 608.

5
00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.442
Excellent choice.

6
00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:09.194
What's the trade?

7
00:01:09.278 --> 00:01:12.823
What would you say to a can of lima beans?

8
00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:16.118
Oh. geez. Bert. come on!
This is near mint.

9
00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:18.745
I could probably get a couple
Dinty Moore Beef Stews for this.

10
00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:20.080
Plus...

11
00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.332
cream corn.

12
00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:26.962
Okay. I was saving it for my birthday.
but I guess I'll throw it in.

13
00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.590
Fancy Feast.

14
00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:31.341
What flavor?

15
00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:33.009
- Salmon.
- Sold.

16
00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.178
- Yay!
- Are you crazy?

17
00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:37.598
Hawkeye doesn't deserve to be an Avenger.

18
00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:39.808
Yeah... Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa!
You do not want to go there.

19
00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.312
You got a guy with a bow and arrow.
and he's supposed to be on the same team

20
00:01:43.395 --> 00:01:47.774
as a guy with an Arc Reactor iron suit
and the literal God of Thunder?

21
00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:49.109
What sense does that even make?

22
00:01:49.192 --> 00:01:52.070
I don't know. I mean...
Does this make sense?

23
00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:59.911
I just mopped! We talked about this. Kyle!

24
00:01:59.995 --> 00:02:03.624
- That's strike three!
- I'm sorry. okay? But you heard him.

25
00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.419
Sorry. He started it.

26
00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:09.378
Unbelievable.

27
00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.632
- Give me a hand.
- Oh. yeah.

28
00:02:11.715 --> 00:02:14.551
You know. I feel the same way
about Green Arrow.

29
00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:16.970
Yeah. we all do
but you don't have to kill people.

30
00:02:20.891 --> 00:02:22.017
Bye!

31
00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.811
- You ever wonder where this thing goes?
- Nope.

32
00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:27.022
- Probably smart.
- Stuart.

33
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:30.901
We gotta talk.

34
00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:34.696
Shit just got weird.

35
00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:13.360
Do you have an identical twin brother?

36
00:03:13.944 --> 00:03:15.070
No.

37
00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:16.988
- Okay. I have two questions.
- Just two?

38
00:03:17.072 --> 00:03:20.075
I've only got a few seconds
to explain this. so you gotta focus.

39
00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:22.202
- Who are you?
- First question.

40
00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:24.996
I'm you from another stream of reality.

41
00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:27.499
Well. that answers that. Second question...

42
00:03:27.582 --> 00:03:28.625
Listen to me.

43
00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:32.587
This apocalyptic nightmare
that you are living in.

44
00:03:32.713 --> 00:03:34.923
it can be avoided. it never has to happen.

45
00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.300
Okay. now I have. like. six questions.

46
00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:39.553
- He can't be me.
- He looks like you.

47
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:42.514
Senior prom. Emily Manhart.
peach schnapps.

48
00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:44.474
She was ready to go. You puked in her lap.

49
00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:45.976
Sounds like you.

50
00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:49.730
- At least I went to my senior prom.
- I couldn't go. I had mono.

51
00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:51.273
Please. I don't have a lot of time.

52
00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:54.651
Leonard Hofstadter.
Sheldon Cooper. Howard Wolowitz.

53
00:03:54.735 --> 00:03:56.903
- Remember them?
- Yeah. real nerds.

54
00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:58.113
Pot-kettle.

55
00:03:58.196 --> 00:03:59.322
- Sure.
- Fair enough.

56
00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:04.911
Anyway. they invented some kind
of quantum entanglement thing.

57
00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:06.830
and you were there when it malfunctioned.

58
00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.081
Both of us or just him?

59
00:04:08.165 --> 00:04:10.250
- Doesn't matter!
- It matters to me.

60
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:14.045
The point is. it altered reality.
None of this is supposed to be.

61
00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:17.591
- And by none of this. you mean...
- None of it!

62
00:04:18.966 --> 00:04:23.430
The violence. the devastation.
the dimensional rifts!

63
00:04:23.513 --> 00:04:26.391
- Dimensional rifts!
- Now we know.

64
00:04:26.475 --> 00:04:28.727
None of this is normal.

65
00:04:31.313 --> 00:04:33.356
- Certainly not that!
- The big moth?

66
00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.526
Yes! Yes! The big moth!

67
00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.029
If you turn the lights off.
they don't bother you.

68
00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:43.450
You can put everything right.
You can make it the way it was.

69
00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:46.495
- You just have to find the...
- Hang on. Hang on!

70
00:04:47.037 --> 00:04:50.916
If you're me from another reality.
how can you be in this one?

71
00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:53.001
I don't know. I'm not a quantum physicist.

72
00:04:53.084 --> 00:04:54.836
I went to the Rhode Island
School of Design.

73
00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.297
- I didn't know that.
- Oh. yeah. I have a BFA.

74
00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.508
Really? How come
you never did anything with it?

75
00:04:59.591 --> 00:05:01.676
What am I gonna do.
teach high school kids how to draw fruit?

76
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.595
Guys. please!

77
00:05:03.678 --> 00:05:06.556
The machine is still at Caltech.
Here's what you have to do.

78
00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.725
Hang on. let me write this down.

79
00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:12.020
"Cal..."

80
00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:13.772
Oh. shoot!

81
00:05:14.356 --> 00:05:17.400
- What is shaking it gonna do?
- Stop talking and listen.

82
00:05:17.484 --> 00:05:19.903
You know.
I might have a Sharpie. excuse me.

83
00:05:21.238 --> 00:05:23.406
Listen!

84
00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:25.617
When you get to the machine...

85
00:05:28.078 --> 00:05:29.788
- Damn it!
- W... What's happening?

86
00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:33.625
I don't know!
I'm going through some kind of wormhole!

87
00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.127
The important thing is...

88
00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:41.675
And... And when you find him...

89
00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:47.973
and that will fix everything.

90
00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:53.478
You get any of that?

91
00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:55.856
I got the gist.

92
00:06:05.323 --> 00:06:06.992
Nice catch. Steve!

93
00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:11.037
- How is it out there?
- It's a little nippy. Wear layers.

94
00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:15.208
Shall we?

95
00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:19.087
I don't know. I'm having second thoughts.

96
00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.882
What are you talking about?
We've been given a quest.

97
00:06:21.965 --> 00:06:25.302
- Yeah. but do we believe that guy?
- That guy was you.

98
00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:28.263
That's my point.
When did we start listening to me?

99
00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:31.266
Maybe we have a chance to fix the world.

100
00:06:31.349 --> 00:06:33.268
I don't know. I think it's important
to ask the question.

101
00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.186
Is this reality that bad?

102
00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.441
I think there's room for improvement.

103
00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:50.493
What are you doing?

104
00:06:51.036 --> 00:06:53.246
What's it look like?
I'm trying to get us to Caltech.

105
00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.748
With a Thomas Guide?

106
00:06:55.248 --> 00:07:00.003
I would've used the GPS on my iPhone.
but civilization seemed to have collapsed.

107
00:07:01.588 --> 00:07:02.672
Check it out.

108
00:07:04.841 --> 00:07:06.009
Juggling two...

109
00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:12.182
Juggling two starving feral creatures.
as you can see. is not difficult. but...

110
00:07:13.475 --> 00:07:18.688
juggling three is... is profoundly stupid.

111
00:07:19.981 --> 00:07:21.733
I saw them in Vegas.

112
00:07:21.816 --> 00:07:23.610
Such a fun night.

113
00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:26.738
You know who I loved in Vegas
and I didn't think I would?

114
00:07:26.821 --> 00:07:28.281
Celine Dion.

115
00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:30.575
I'm sorry.

116
00:07:36.206 --> 00:07:37.207
All right.

117
00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.126
Oh. yeah.

118
00:07:46.091 --> 00:07:47.300
Thank you!

119
00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:51.388
We are Penn and Teller
and we'll be here until we're dead!

120
00:08:08.029 --> 00:08:09.072
Moth.

121
00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:17.580
Oh. my God. look. Floss.

122
00:08:17.664 --> 00:08:20.709
- Just hurry. It's getting dark.
- Yeah. yeah. yeah.

123
00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:23.712
Excuse me. how much for a foot of floss?

124
00:08:23.795 --> 00:08:26.381
- Mint or regular?
- Let me get the regular.

125
00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:35.390
Thank you. Oh. yeah. look at that.

126
00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.351
Can't put a price on healthy gums.

127
00:08:41.229 --> 00:08:45.984
- This feels so good.
- Go easy. We're sharing that.

128
00:08:48.778 --> 00:08:49.904
Not a good sound.

129
00:08:53.158 --> 00:08:54.367
Stuart?

130
00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:56.911
Denise?

131
00:08:56.995 --> 00:08:59.497
- I thought you were dead.
- I thought you were dead!

132
00:09:00.915 --> 00:09:03.126
So. what have you been up to?

133
00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.628
Robbing mostly.
Still working on my screenplay.

134
00:09:05.712 --> 00:09:07.922
- Good for you.
- Yeah. How have you been?

135
00:09:08.006 --> 00:09:10.508
- Okay. Still got the store.
- That's great.

136
00:09:10.592 --> 00:09:11.593
What's going on?

137
00:09:12.302 --> 00:09:13.803
Don't worry. Gary. I know these guys.

138
00:09:13.887 --> 00:09:16.347
So. we're not robbing. we're not killing?
What are we doing?

139
00:09:16.431 --> 00:09:20.268
- You remember I mentioned Stuart?
- Sure. How's it going? Gary.

140
00:09:20.351 --> 00:09:21.394
Hi.

141
00:09:22.353 --> 00:09:24.064
So. are you two...

142
00:09:24.147 --> 00:09:26.232
You gotta remember.
I thought you were dead.

143
00:09:26.316 --> 00:09:28.234
Yeah. no. right. right. yeah.

144
00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:30.737
Funny story. actually.
Gary was seeing my friend Lisa.

145
00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.322
Nice girl. Yeah. Jewish.

146
00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:35.742
Yeah. and anyway. Lisa got eaten
by cannibals in Sherman Oaks.

147
00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:37.535
Oh. no.

148
00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:39.412
Human meat isn't kosher.

149
00:09:39.496 --> 00:09:42.832
but I guess that only matters
if the cannibals are also Jewish.

150
00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:48.254
Anyway. we. you know.
comforted each other.

151
00:09:48.379 --> 00:09:50.673
- The lady has skills. am I right?
- Well...

152
00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:55.220
To be honest.
I mostly focused on my own performance.

153
00:09:56.763 --> 00:10:00.892
- Anyway. we gotta go.
- Yeah. Caltech. We're on a quest.

154
00:10:00.975 --> 00:10:03.853
There's no more Caltech.
What's left of it is a death trap.

155
00:10:03.937 --> 00:10:05.105
We don't have a choice.

156
00:10:05.188 --> 00:10:07.732
Yeah. an alternate version of me
came from another universe

157
00:10:07.816 --> 00:10:09.776
and explained
how I can undo the apocalypse.

158
00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:13.154
- It was really cool.
- An alternate version of you?

159
00:10:13.238 --> 00:10:15.615
Yeah. same pasty face
and same whiny voice.

160
00:10:15.698 --> 00:10:17.033
It was like looking in a mirror.

161
00:10:17.117 --> 00:10:19.410
Well. good luck.

162
00:10:19.494 --> 00:10:22.205
- Yeah. nice to see you.
- Yeah. you too.

163
00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:25.542
Have fun with the... looting and stuff.

164
00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:27.919
Ciao.

165
00:10:31.589 --> 00:10:34.425
- They're gonna die.
- Oh. yeah.

166
00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:44.269
- That looks bad.
- Because of all the guns?

167
00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.272
Yes. because of all the guns.

168
00:10:50.108 --> 00:10:53.778
- Denise. what are you doing?
- Trying to keep you alive.

169
00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.197
I don't care about your life.
I'm just hoping to get laid tonight.

170
00:10:56.281 --> 00:10:57.282
Gary.

171
00:10:57.365 --> 00:10:58.366
- Very kind.
- Thank you.

172
00:10:58.449 --> 00:11:00.994
- What's your plan?
- No. I don't really have one.

173
00:11:01.077 --> 00:11:03.830
- I'm kind of new to the action genre.
- All right. here's how we do this.

174
00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:05.373
I'll create a distraction
at the main gate.

175
00:11:05.456 --> 00:11:07.917
The three of you cut around to the side
where the trucks are going in.

176
00:11:07.959 --> 00:11:09.002
Yeah. then what?

177
00:11:09.085 --> 00:11:13.464
When the trucks stop. you roll under them.
grab the undercarriage. and ride on in.

178
00:11:13.548 --> 00:11:15.508
You. sir. have done this before.

179
00:11:15.592 --> 00:11:17.594
Well. back in the day.
I was Army Special Forces.

180
00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:20.096
Cool. I was a geologist.

181
00:11:21.639 --> 00:11:22.807
- We ready?
- Yeah.

182
00:11:22.891 --> 00:11:28.396
- Hang on. So... So. roll. run. grab?
- Run. roll. grab.

183
00:11:28.479 --> 00:11:33.860
- Sorry. more of a visual learner.
- On three. One. two. three!

184
00:11:36.279 --> 00:11:37.614
Oh. my God. Gary!

185
00:11:37.697 --> 00:11:40.033
- Don't move!
- Hands in the air!

186
00:11:43.119 --> 00:11:46.456
Tell them
about the alternate version of you.

187
00:11:47.457 --> 00:11:49.000
Oh. my gosh. Gary.

188
00:11:49.083 --> 00:11:52.212
It's terrible. Just terrible.
But you know what?

189
00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:54.380
You... You're gonna find somebody else.

190
00:11:55.131 --> 00:11:56.799
Maybe sooner than you think.

191
00:11:58.051 --> 00:11:59.177
Get in there!

192
00:12:00.929 --> 00:12:03.223
- Wow!
- What?

193
00:12:03.306 --> 00:12:05.725
This used to be my Geology classroom.

194
00:12:06.351 --> 00:12:09.479
- I opened so many young minds here.
- Can you keep it down?

195
00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.148
Raj?

196
00:12:14.525 --> 00:12:16.110
Maybe. Possibly.

197
00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:18.154
Who wants to know?

198
00:12:18.947 --> 00:12:21.241
Raj. it's me. Stuart.
from the comic book store.

199
00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:25.119
Stuart?

200
00:12:25.203 --> 00:12:28.414
Yes. and... and Bert Kibbler.
You know Bert?

201
00:12:28.498 --> 00:12:31.000
- Bert?
- And Denise. Remember Denise?

202
00:12:33.544 --> 00:12:36.172
This isn't real.
This is... This is a hallucination!

203
00:12:36.256 --> 00:12:38.508
No. No. no. no. We're here. It's real.

204
00:12:38.591 --> 00:12:41.094
That's kind of what
a hallucination would say.

205
00:12:42.845 --> 00:12:46.140
- What are you doing here?
- Isn't it obvious? I'm in a locked room.

206
00:12:46.224 --> 00:12:49.018
I haven't changed my underwear in years.
and I crap in a bucket!

207
00:12:50.311 --> 00:12:51.604
So. you're like a prisoner?

208
00:12:51.688 --> 00:12:54.983
I rode an elephant to my wedding
and now I crap in a bucket!

209
00:12:55.066 --> 00:12:56.276
Congratulations.

210
00:12:57.402 --> 00:13:00.238
- On the wedding thing.
- Yeah. a moth ate her.

211
00:13:01.155 --> 00:13:05.827
Anyway. I... I've had time
to... to... to figure it all out.

212
00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.663
and there's definitely something wrong
with this reality.

213
00:13:08.746 --> 00:13:12.750
See? I prove it here and here.
and the numbers. they don't lie.

214
00:13:12.834 --> 00:13:15.086
- So. you were telling the truth?
- You didn't believe me?

215
00:13:15.169 --> 00:13:17.380
That an alternate version of you
told you how to save the universe?

216
00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.007
No. not for a minute.

217
00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:23.553
Pay attention!
Leonard. Sheldon. and Howard.

218
00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:27.307
They built a vari-state
quantum interference device.

219
00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:28.766
That would have been my guess.

220
00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.811
It malfunctioned.
and it changed everything. right?

221
00:13:31.894 --> 00:13:34.605
The universe. history. reality.

222
00:13:34.689 --> 00:13:36.649
Yeah. yeah. great.
How... How do we fix it?

223
00:13:36.733 --> 00:13:39.110
Yeah. that's a toughie. Why. you ask?

224
00:13:39.777 --> 00:13:41.779
Wait. did you ask? I assume you ask.

225
00:13:41.863 --> 00:13:46.117
It's a toughie because we're all prisoners
of the Evil One.

226
00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:52.123
And the Evil One likes everything
to stay just as it is.

227
00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:54.834
Who's the Evil One?

228
00:13:56.878 --> 00:14:00.131
I can't say his name!
If I say his name. bad things happen.

229
00:14:01.632 --> 00:14:02.925
Sorry. is it Voldemort?

230
00:14:03.009 --> 00:14:05.053
I wish it was Voldemort.
That's a guy you can reason with.

231
00:14:05.136 --> 00:14:06.220
But...

232
00:14:06.846 --> 00:14:09.724
If we got to the device.
you could really reset the universe?

233
00:14:09.807 --> 00:14:11.851
Bing. bang. boom! But it's hopeless!

234
00:14:11.934 --> 00:14:14.979
That device.
it's surrounded by armed guards. 24/7!

235
00:14:15.063 --> 00:14:17.398
No. it's not hopeless.
The alternate me said

236
00:14:17.482 --> 00:14:19.484
that I'm the chosen one
who'll set things right.

237
00:14:20.276 --> 00:14:21.694
He didn't say "chosen."

238
00:14:21.778 --> 00:14:26.741
- Well. he implied "chosen."
- Boy. I did not get that at all.

239
00:14:27.408 --> 00:14:28.743
All kneel...

240
00:14:28.826 --> 00:14:32.789
for the Grand Caliph of South Pasadena.
Flintridge. and Monrovia!

241
00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:35.540
The Supreme Ruler
of the San Gabriel Valley!

242
00:14:35.625 --> 00:14:37.126
I'm not kneeling for anybody!

243
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.587
Okay. yeah.

244
